<title>BELARUS: Belarus bans meat exports, butter/margarine import.</title>
<headline>Belarus bans meat exports, butter/margarine import.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belarus has temporarily banned exports of meat and imports of butter and margarine, the Deputy Minister of Agriculture said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The ban on meat exports is tied with an earlier ban on imported meat due to diseased cattle in Western countries,&quot; Ivan Shakolo said at a news conference, adding that the nationwide export ban would probably be in effect until June.</p>
<p>But he added it would not apply to Russian enterprises providing grain to Belarus in exchange for meat payments.</p>
<p>&quot;The ban on butter and margarine imports will be in effect until at least October, and its goal is to protect our producers. We have enough resources to fully meet the needs of the republic,&quot; Shakolo said.</p>
<p>--Kiev Newsroom +380 44 244-9150</p>
</text>
